    "title": "New Haven boys, Warsaw girls win on Wednesday - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Glenn Marini No media credit provided. ,\n1 hours ago\nFORT WAYNE, Ind. (WANE) – New Haven edged 3-time defending SAC champ Wayne in boys basketball while 4A no. 5 Warsaw dispatched Carroll in girls action to headline the area prep hoops scene on Wednesday night.\nTarvar Baskerville led New Haven with 24 points as the Bulldogs beat Wayne on the road by a score of 74-70. The Bulldogs are now 3-1 on the season with their next game at home against Bellmont on Friday, Dec. 19 in the NE8 opener for both clubs. Wayne falls to 1-1 on the season and will host Snider in their SAC opener on Friday.\nAt Charger Fieldhouse Warsaw improved to 9-1 overall with a 73-29 victory over host Carroll. Brooke Zartman led the Tigers with 26 points, while Joslyn Bricker added 21 and Alexis Neely 10. Lily George led Carroll with 13 points while Ava Myers chipped in with 12.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WANE 15.",
